[Retroactive note added later, per the Symptom/Ruled out/Root cause/Fix commit-message framework]

Symptom: in-game menu shortcuts (Cmd+A, Cmd+Z) weren't registering at all.

Root cause: confirmed by reading Wine's actual source (not guessed) —
Whisky's forked Wine (winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m) injects a hidden "Edit"
menu into every Wine window, bound to Cmd+X/C/V/A/Z. macOS matches that
menu's key equivalents before the keypress ever reaches the game, so
Cmd+A/Cmd+Z specifically get swallowed. Already reported upstream:
Whisky-App/Whisky#1060.

Fix: disabled the hidden Edit menu via the Mac Driver registry
(`EditMenu` key).

Note: this fix was later found to have a real side-effect cost and was
superseded — see 59b7be7's note for what broke and why.
